  "title": "Garamantian foggara irrigation in the Fazzan",
  "summary": "The Garamantes of the Fazzan in southwest Libya irrigated desert oases with foggara, underground canals that carried aquifer water by gravity. EBSCO dates their civilization to c. 500 BCE-c. 200 CE and describes a 3,000-mile network. Archaeology magazine links foggara mastery to population growth, towns and conquest.",
